        <mxCell id="enum_Language" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Arial;fillColor=#FFF8E1;strokeColor=#8D6E63;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-top:4px;text-align:center;font-size:11px;&quot;&gt;«enumeration»&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;text-align:center;font-size:13px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Language&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:6px;line-height:16px;&quot;&gt;Vietnamese&lt;br&gt;English&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1784" width="185" height="84" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="enum_TokenPurpose" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Arial;fillColor=#FFF8E1;strokeColor=#8D6E63;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-top:4px;text-align:center;font-size:11px;&quot;&gt;«enumeration»&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;text-align:center;font-size:13px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TokenPurpose&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:6px;line-height:16px;&quot;&gt;AccountSetup&lt;br&gt;PasswordReset&lt;br&gt;EmailVerification&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="240" y="1784" width="185" height="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFF9E6;strokeColor=#D6B656;fontSize=12;" value="&lt;b&gt;Notation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;◆ composition (the part cannot exist without the whole)&lt;br&gt;◇ aggregation (the part can exist on its own)&lt;br&gt;plain line = association&lt;br&gt;- private &amp;nbsp;+ public &amp;nbsp;·&amp;nbsp; [0..1] = optional value&lt;br&gt;&lt;u&gt;underlined&lt;/u&gt; = class-level (static) operation&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mapping to the ERD&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every ERD entity has a class of the same name. Role is a class of its own: every user has exactly one role (Student, Lecturer or Administrator), and the role decides what the user may do; the API layer checks it before each operation. User holds the person (name, username, student/lecturer code, class); UserAccount holds how they sign in (account name, email, Google link, salt + password hash). Every user has exactly one account.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rubric and AI scores&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A rubric is a list of criteria; its maxScore is the sum of their maxPoints. For each answered question the AI gives every criterion a CriterionScore; QuestionResponse.aiSuggestedScore is their sum, kept with the AI feedback.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Final score&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A ScoreReview starts as Pending, at the sum of the AI-suggested scores. The score counts as confirmed only when its status is Approved (the attempt is then Finalized). A question not reached before the session closes has no QuestionResponse and counts as 0.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Not shown as operations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Log in and Log out run in the API layer (Authentication, JWT); the classes keep only the data they use, all in UserAccount: accountName, email, passwordHash, passwordSalt and googleLinked. Read-only views (exam report, student results, class statistics, audit log, reviewing an attempt) are queries in the API layer. TTS, STT, follow-up generation and rubric scoring run in the AI adapters; the classes keep their results (InterviewTurn, CriterionScore, QuestionResponse)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1420" y="1382" width="840" height="400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" value="AIVES – Class Diagram" vertex="1">
